  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "Step 1 was incomplete: I added wire3 to wire7. The manual's 12V power schematic (VIN/GND screw block, relay, pump) needs wires, and the image wasn't given. I assumed the usual wiring: 12V+ to carrier VIN, 12V- to carrier GND, VIN to relay COM, relay NO to pump +, pump - to GND.",
   "The carrier catalogue entry lists no ports. I named them 'A0.1'..'A0.4', 'D0.n', 'D1.n' and 'TWI.n' for each Grove connector's pins (1=SIG/SCL, 2=NC/SDA, 3=VCC, 4=GND), plus 'VCC', 'VIN' and 'GND' for the supply and screw block.",
   "Grove pin order is SIG/SCL, NC/SDA, VCC, GND. The NC pin of the single-signal modules is left unconnected.",
   "The MKR Zero has no SDA/SCL ports in my new type, so I used its I2C pins D11 (SDA) and D12 (SCL) for the TWI connector.",
   "The two solid wires are soldered to two unconnected tinned bars of the water sensor. The sensor has no port for individual bars, so those edges use null ports.",
   "The wall adapter's tip/sleeve are wired to the screw terminals through wires, assumed to be stripped leads from the barrel jack.",
   "The Grove relay's NC_CONTACT is unused. The relay is driven from the carrier's 3.3V Grove connector, as the manual describes.",
   "The MKR Zero is powered over USB for programming. In use, the 12V supply feeds it through the carrier's VIN."
  ]
 },
